Description: Detect phrases and the first downbeat of tracks without rekordbox data
 AnalyzerPhrases (after AnalyzerBeats in the analyzer pipeline) fills the
 track structure of patch 0007 for tracks that have no rekordbox phrases, so
 the phrase band, the bar counter and phrase-aligned Auto DJ work for every
 track. Inspired by upstream PRs #16582 (energy novelty quantized to bars)
 and #17404 (loudness + bass change around each beat, bar phase from the
 beats where the changes peak); no code is taken from them unchanged.
 .
 While decoding: mean square of the signal and of a 150 Hz biquad low-pass
 per 512 frames. After the beats are known: loudness and bass level (dB)
 per beat; change score = |loudness change| + |bass change| between the 16
 beats before and from each beat (8 at least, within the range with sound).
 Bar phase (if there is no rekordbox downbeat): the beat offset mod 4 on
 which the change peaks fall. First phrase from the first downbeat with
 sound. Bars where the score peaks above 3 dB become boundaries; a broad
 peak moves one bar onto the 8/4-bar grid (the grid offset is the bar mod 8
 of the changes) if the score there is at least 90 % of the peak;
 boundaries closer than 4 bars are merged (the stronger one stays);
 sections longer than 32 bars are cut into 16-bar pieces. Labels use the
 rekordbox "High" mood names: first Intro, last Outro, others Chorus if
 their level (mean of loudness and bass dB) is within 3 dB of the loudest
 middle section, Down if more than 6 dB below it, Up in between.
 .
 TrackStructure gets a source (rekordbox or detected), serialization
 version 2; version 1 data is read as rekordbox data. A detected structure
 never replaces rekordbox phrases (checked under the track lock); the
 rekordbox import paths replace a detected structure. A rekordbox first
 downbeat without phrases is kept. The analyzer runs on load / batch
 analysis for tracks without a structure even if beats and waveform exist
 (only this analyzer decodes the file then), and again when the beats are
 detected again. [Library],DetectPhrases=0 switches it off. Results were
 only tested with synthetic levels and synthetic audio.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
